{"availability":"available","full":"victor-onoja/degenChess","name":"degenChess","description":"DegenChess is a copy of the regular chess game but with a web3 twist. ","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2024-09-21T14:29:16Z","updated":"2026-10-10T10:33:21Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://degen-chess.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://degen-chess.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.221Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.221Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.221Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.221Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Renamed from the working title DegenChess on 5 October 2026. Testnet: (mainnet will be awaychess.com). The game contract (contracts/DegenChess.sol), browser storage keys and the repo keep the old name; the first address, degen-chess.vercel.app, still serves the same app, but accounts are per address.","Staked chess on-chain. Both players put up the same dollar stake, and every capture moves that piece's value from the victim to the capturer. When the game ends, the winner takes the loser's balance except what the loser earned through their own captures, so a loser who fought well still gets paid.","Tech stack: Next.js, Mera passkey accounts, viem/wagmi, react-chessboard, chess.js, Solidity (Hardhat), on Monad testnet. Stakes are in tUSD, a 6-decimal test dollar standing in for AUSD."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/victor-onoja/degenChess/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"7fcb567dc23fb05fe784c6b99ecaf71340c6e1ba8cbf3c6d5e1f163b70eb79e0","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.305Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.305Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Renamed from the working title DegenChess on 5 October 2026. Testnet: (mainnet will be awaychess.com). The game contract (contracts/DegenChess.sol), browser storage keys an